Using a json api as a web service is a general method that is used in many, many applications. I don't think anyone holds exclusive rights to do this. I have been using json R web services long before revolution had their product (as shown on my useR 2009 <http://www.r-project.org/conferences/useR-2009/slides/Ooms.pdf> slides), so I cannot imagine that they suddenly consider this as infringement.

Also note that 'copyright' only applies to actual source code. You cannot hold copyright to a method or technique.

